Cell[TextData[{
 "Now we define the two dipole-exit-to-dipole-entrance matrices (i.e. purely \
consisting of drifts and quadrupoles) and apply the achromatic condition \
(which constraints ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["m", "12"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "286b7cf9-a262-4167-97cc-48c639b300d6"],
 "and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["m", "22"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f004e67b-afb6-4e89-988d-8e2ef40167b6"],
 ").  We are doing this as we want to get A, B, C and D in terms of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["m", "11"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "729e07f3-a74e-4d36-8291-8c81af629813"],
 "and the dipole parameters."
}], "Text",
